  "findings": {
    "confirmed": [
      "Four runs on four different groups, one account 9757, workflow 1, block 34, positions 1/2/3, commentType=all and commentGroupMode=all.",
      "Three complete successful comment steps in run 4876305; nine commentFailed=true steps on three other runs. Step status alone is success even for handled comment failures.",
      "All nine failure errors contain the updated element 13 XPath with contains(@aria-label,'Comment'); each fails in about 8.7-9.3 seconds.",
      "Two failed runs report pending post URLs. One failed run and the successful run both report pending_content_empty and isPending=false.",
      "The nonpending failed run starts comment 8.819 seconds after form-close verification; the successful one starts after 8.750 seconds.",
      "The three comment text hashes match across all four runs; configured comment iterations and comment media configuration hashes also match.",
      "Failure imageCount=0 is downstream of failure before upload; successful steps report imageCount=1.",
      "No run events or screenshots are stored for the four compared run IDs."
    ],
    "source_findings": [
      "Live block 34 waits 8000ms for element13 before click, then waits for dialog textbox1517. It does not navigate to the postUrl.",
      "Live block2627 preserves positions1..3 for pending posts with commentType=all and commentGroupMode=all; this is intended current semantics.",
      "Current pageController filters style/size visibility before applying the trailing numeric XPath index and scrolls the window every three unsuccessful polls within the existing timeout.",
      "Current scheduler checks my_pending_content in a temporary page and destroys it; the main comment page is not navigated there.",
      "Current commentUrl extraction reads the first comment permalink and is not an identity proof of the newly submitted comment."
    ],
    "not_proven": [
      "Exact DOM, active URL, dialog state, matching node count and visibility at each failed lookup were not captured.",
      "Cannot distinguish unloaded DOM, hidden matching nodes, group-specific selector attributes or another transient page state using these stored logs.",
      "No per-run client version or cached successful selector is captured; all nine errors demonstrably use the new selector, and live block/element definitions are unchanged.",
      "Pending status alone and high n do not explain all nine failures."
    ]
  },
